course: dictionary
lesson: 3411
title: Words that show how something happens
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Explosively is an adverb, so it tells you how something happens. Its main meaning is in a sudden, loud and violent way, like an explosion. «The balloon burst explosively» tells you the balloon went pop in one sudden, loud rush.
explain: The same word can also mean very fast and full of energy, especially at the start. «The sprinter started explosively» means the runner went off the mark all at once, not slowly.
explain: It can also describe a sudden angry reaction. «He reacted explosively» shows he lost his temper quickly, not calmly.
explain: To work out which meaning fits, read the words around it. A bang, a rush or a sudden start are clues. Then swap in your meaning and check the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Explosively is an adverb: it describes how something happens.
fact: «Explosively» means in a sudden, loud and violent way, like an explosion.
fact: «Explosively» can also mean very fast and full of energy, especially at the start.
fact: «Explosively» can describe a sudden angry reaction, as in «He reacted explosively».
fact: Shake up a fizzy drink and the gas rushes out and drags the drink with it. Sticky magma full of gas erupts explosively the same way, while runny magma lets its gas escape and just pours out.
exercise: «The balloon burst explosively.» What does explosively mean here? | Slowly and gently | Very quietly, without any noise | Under the water | *With a sudden, loud bang
exercise: «The sprinter started explosively.» What does explosively suggest? | Without moving at all | Late, after everyone else | Sadly and slowly | *With great speed and energy from the very start
exercise: «He reacted explosively.» Which word is closest in meaning? | Calmly | Sleepily | *Angrily, with a sudden outburst | Happily
test: Her coach shouts, «Push off explosively!» What does the coach want? | A slow walk to the line | A gentle stop | *A strong, fast start | A rest before the race
test: Sticky magma full of gas erupts explosively. What does explosively mean here? | Slowly, in a steady trickle | Quietly, like a drip from a tap | *With a sudden, violent blast | Cold and hard
exam: Why does runny magma not erupt explosively? | It has no gas at all in it | It is too cold to move | *Its gas escapes easily, so it pours out instead of blasting | It is frozen solid
